            <ArticleTitle>Flurbiprofen-associated acute tubulointerstitial nephritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>144-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of biopsy-proven acute tubulointerstitial nephritis associated with a second course of flurbiprofen, a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug of the propionic acid class. The clinical presentation and course was consistent with acute tubulointerstitial nephritis due to these agents.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
